            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0534" n="446" xml:id="pg446"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/953: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-02T13:00:00-06:00">February 2, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Referring to Department’s circular telegram February 1, 7 p.m., 1933.
                    Notwithstanding Mexico has no diplomatic relations with Peru (see my telegram
                    90, May 25, 7 p.m., and Department’s instruction 671, May 28, 1932<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d434-f1"/>) I discreetly interviewed the Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    this morning, who confirmed the impression I previously had, that owing to the
                    fact that Mexico has no diplomatic relations with Peru it is not possible for
                    Mexico to make any representations to Peru on this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
